<p class="mission">To what extent do informed decisions beat ill-informed ones? <span class="q">What if you could bring a whole lifetime of data to bear on every decision in your life?</span></p>

<p class="submission">We all leave a trail of data behind us; smartwatches, banks, inboxes, medical files. What if you claimed the lot and put modern algorithms to work on it? Could a machine learn what you actually do, and why? Could it take a goal you bring, fit the way of reaching it to you, show what it would take, and hand the schlep to software?</p>

<p class="submission">Eudaemon is one person finding out. The archive is <b>the lakes</b>; the analysis that tries to understand is <b>the deep twin</b>; the machinery that turns a goal into a method fitted to the person is <b>Telos</b>; the arm that does the schlep is <b>Jarvis</b>.</p>

